{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Circumcise the foreskin of your heart.</b> If so, it is fitting that you remove the foreskin of your intellect — that is, that you reflect to remove every error that gives rise to false opinions." "<b>And your neck you shall not stiffen any more.</b> And by removing the stiffness of the neck that prevents one from turning toward what is fitting, you shall turn to know your Creator and see that it is evil and bitter to forsake Him — and this is through your reflection."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:05.699857019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}